#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:57
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kpackage; is a &GUI; interface to the <acronym>SMART</acronym> package "
"manager. &kpackage; is part of the K Desktop Environment and, as a result, "
"it is designed to integrate with the &kde; file manager."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid "Onscreen Fundamentals"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:70
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kpackage; has two panels. The left panel displays a tree of the installed "
"and available packages, the right panel displays information on the packages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Main Window - Package Tree"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:78
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When &kpackage; is started normally (that is it has not been invoked via "
"drag and drop and has not been given any parameters) it displays two panels "
"with the package tree on the left, this tree shows installed and available "
"packages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:84
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Left Panel"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:89
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Left Panel - Package Tree</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:92
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Left Panel - Package Tree</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "The left panel displays the list of packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Search:</guilabel> line filters the package tree so that only "
"those packages whose name or summary contains the search string are "
"displayed. The columns that are searched can be changed by a menu that can "
"be brought up by clicking the &RMB; on the search line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Next to the search line is a pull down menu that filters the displayed "
"packages based on status:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Installed Packages</guilabel> - Show packages that have been "
"installed"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>New Packages</guilabel> - Show uninstalled packages that are new "
"or have been updated"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Updated Packages</guilabel> - Show installed packages for which "
"newer versions are available"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Available Packages</guilabel> - Show uninstalled packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:112
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>All Packages</guilabel> - All packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The package tree is based on the sections of the distribution and shows "
"summary information about the packages:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Package</guilabel> - Name of the package"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Mark</guilabel> - Shows a tick if the package has been marked. "
"Marking allows multiple packages to be installed or uninstalled at once "
"using the buttons located below the package tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Summary</guilabel> - A short description of the package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:125
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Size</guilabel> - The package size"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Version</guilabel> - The package version"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guilabel>Old Version</guilabel> - If the package updates an installed "
"package, the version of the old package"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The packages have graphical labels to indicate their state, an image "
"representing the package type means an installed package, a <guilabel>N</"
"guilabel> indicates an available package and a <guilabel>U</guilabel> means "
"a package that can upgrade an installed package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:137
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A single package is selected by clicking on the name. Clicking on the dot in "
"the <guilabel>Mark</guilabel> column marks the package with a tick, a second "
"click unmarks it, while <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<mousebutton>left</"
"mousebutton></keycombo> click can be used to mark a range of packages and "
"<keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<mousebutton>left</mousebutton></keycombo> "
"click can be used to add and remove marks on packages."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting a package from the tree displays information about it in the right "
"panel."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:151
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Main Window - Package Information Panel"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The right panel has tabs for displaying four different types of information "
"about selected packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:159
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Right Panel - Properties"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:164
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right Panel - Package Properties"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Properties</guilabel> tab which displays information on the "
"selected package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:177
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Right Panel - Dependencies"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right Panel - The Depenencies for the Package"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Dependencies List</guilabel> tab shows the Dependencies and "
"Provides for the package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Right Panel - Files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:200 index.docbook:222
#, no-c-format
msgid "Right Panel - The Files in the Package"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>File List</guilabel> tab shows the files in the package and "
"for installed packages (provided the information is available) shows the "
"state of the files. Files that exist are marked with a tick, those that are "
"missing are marked with a cross."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:217
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Right Panel - Change Log"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:225
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Change Log</guilabel> tab shows the change log for the package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid "Installing Packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:240
#, no-c-format
msgid "To install a package you can"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:243
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"locate the package you wish to install in &konqueror;, drag it onto a "
"running copy of &kpackage;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"click on a package file in &konqueror; and start a new copy of &kpackage;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:251
#, no-c-format
msgid "use on the <guimenu>Open</guimenu> menu items in &kpackage;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:255
#, no-c-format
msgid "selecting an available package in the package tree"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For a selected package, use the <guibutton>Install</guibutton> button pops "
"up the installation window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For marked packages, use the <guibutton>Install Marked</guibutton> button on "
"the left panel, which pops up the install window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:269
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Install dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:274
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Install Dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:277
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Install Dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:282
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Install</guilabel> dialog lists the packages to be selected to "
"be installed in a panel in the top left as well the packages needed to "
"satisfy any dependencies. The selected packages have check boxes that allows "
"their installation to be disabled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:286
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Install</guibutton> button will start the actual install. "
"Normally the install window will be deleted after a successful install but "
"if the <guibutton>Keep this window</guibutton> check box is selected the "
"window will stay around."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:292
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The panel on the right is an integrated terminal window in which the "
"installation programs are run, for interactive installation programs the "
"interaction is done in this window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:300
#, no-c-format
msgid "Uninstalling Packages"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:302
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A selected package can be uninstalled by using the <guibutton>Uninstall</"
"guibutton> button in the right panel, the <guibutton>Uninstall Marked</"
"guibutton> in the left panel can be used to uninstall marked packages. The "
"buttons bring up the <guilabel>Uninstall</guilabel> dialog."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:309
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Uninstall dialog"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:314
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Uninstall Dialog</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:317
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Uninstall Dialog</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guibutton>Uninstall</guibutton> button in the window causes the "
"packages to be uninstalled, and the right panel provides an integrated "
"terminal window for the uninstall program."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:331
#, no-c-format
msgid "Searching"
msgstr "Recèrca"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid "Package Search Line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:336
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Search Line"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Search Line</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:344
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Search Line</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The Search line filters the package tree so that only those packages whose "
"name or summary contains the search string are displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:354
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Find Package</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:357
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Find Package"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:362
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Find Package</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:365
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Find Package</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:370
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Find Package</guilabel> dialog searches the names of the "
"packages in the package tree and moves to the next matching package. If "
"<guilabel>Sub string</guilabel> is not set then it will find only exact "
"matches against packages names. If <guilabel>Wrap search</guilabel> is not "
"set the search doesn't wrap around the end of the package tree."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:379
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Find File</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:382
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Find File"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:387
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Find File</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:390
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Find File</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:395
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guilabel>Find File</guilabel> dialog searches for files the names of "
"which contain the search string. The columns in the display are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:400
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Installed</guilabel> - Ticked if it is an installed package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:403
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Type</guilabel> - The type of the package."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:406
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Package</guilabel> - The name of the package"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:409
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>File Name</guilabel> - The name of the matched file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:412
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Only the files in installed packages are shown unless <guilabel>Also search "
"uninstalled packages</guilabel> is set, this will only work if the "
"<command>apt-file</command> command is installed. The database used by the "
"<command>apt-file</command> command is updated by the <guimenuitem>Apt-File "
"Update</guimenuitem> menu item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:423
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Misc</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:425
#, no-c-format
msgid "Root Access"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:427
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kpackage; requires <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> access "
"for installing/uninstalling packages, this can be can be done by running "
"&kpackage; as <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem>, say by using "
"&kdesu;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:432
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Alternatively, if &kpackage; is running as a normal user it will try to run "
"the install/uninstall programs as root by logging in to a pseudo terminal, "
"it will use either <command>su</command>, <command>sudo</command> or "
"<command>ssh</command> to do this and if needed it will pop up a prompt "
"window where the <systemitem class=\"username\">root</systemitem> password "
"or <command>ssh</command> key can be typed. For this to work the root prompt "
"has to end in <prompt># </prompt>. The <guimenuitem>Remember password</"
"guimenuitem> option causes &kpackage; to remember the password that is "
"entered."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:441
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kpackage; Password prompt"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:446
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>Password prompt</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:449
#, no-c-format
msgid "<para>Password prompt</para>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:458
#, no-c-format
msgid "Drag and Drop"
msgstr "Rossegar e pausar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:460
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kpackage; makes use of the &kde; Drag and Drop protocol. This means that "
"you can drag and drop packages onto &kpackage; to open them. Dropping a file "
"onto the <guilabel>Find File</guilabel> dialog will find the package that "
"contains the file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:471
#, no-c-format
msgid "Menus"
msgstr "Menuts"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:473
#, no-c-format
msgid "This describes the &kpackage; menus."
msgstr ""

